<% layout('base') -%>
<section class="intro">
  <div class="container intro__grid">
    <div class="intro__description">
      <p class="eyebrow">Web-based business tools.</p>

      <h1>You own the data.</h1>

      <p>
        Manage your customers, employees, jobs, inventory, sales, estimates,
        invoices, payments, and other business records in one application.
      </p>

      <p>
        Each tool works from the same business records, keeping information
        connected as it moves between customers, jobs, inventory, employees,
        sales, and accounting.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our network allows your employees and customers to access information
        that you own without requiring a monthly software subscription or
        forcing changes to the version you use.
      </p>

      <div class="intro__links">
        <a href="/features"> Features → </a>

        <a href="/demo"> Demo → </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="software-check">
      <header class="software-check__header">
        <span>YOUR CURRENT SOFTWARE</span>

        <span class="software-check__count"> 1 / 5 </span>
      </header>

      <div class="software-check__body">
        <p class="software-check__question">
          Has a program you use changed its interface or workflow without giving
          you the option to keep the version you already knew?
        </p>

        <div class="software-check__answers">
          <button type="button" data-answer="yes">Yes</button>

          <button type="button" data-answer="no">No</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-section">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="product-section__header">
      <span>01</span>

      <div>
        <h2>What it is</h2>

        <p>
          A web application for storing and working with the information used to
          operate a business.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="product-list">
      <article>
        <h3>Customers</h3>
        <p>
          Contact information, locations, jobs, estimates, invoices, payments,
          notes, and history.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Jobs</h3>
        <p>
          Work orders, assigned employees, tasks, materials, status, notes, and
          related customer records.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Inventory</h3>
        <p>
          Products, parts, quantities, costs, pricing, purchasing, and usage.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Employees</h3>
        <p>
          Employee accounts, roles, permissions, assigned work, and access to
          the parts of the application they need.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Sales & Billing</h3>
        <p>
          Estimates, invoices, payments, point-of-sale transactions,
          receivables, and basic payables.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Customer Access</h3>
        <p>
          Customer-facing access to invoices, estimates, payments, and other
          information that a business chooses to make available.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-section product-section--dark">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="product-section__header">
      <span>02</span>

      <div>
        <h2>How the software is sold</h2>

        <p>Purchasing software should not mean renting it indefinitely.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="version-example">
      <div class="version-example__item">
        <span class="version-example__version"> INVENTORY 1 </span>

        <h3>Your current version</h3>

        <p>
          You purchased it. It works. You can continue using it without an
          update changing how it behaves.
        </p>

        <span class="version-example__status"> OWNED </span>
      </div>

      <div class="version-example__arrow">→</div>

      <div class="version-example__item">
        <span class="version-example__version"> INVENTORY 2 </span>

        <h3>A later version</h3>

        <p>
          A finished revision may add features, change the interface, or improve
          how inventory is handled.
        </p>

        <p>
          You can purchase it if those changes are useful. If they are not, keep
          version 1.
        </p>

        <span class="version-example__status"> OPTIONAL </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-section">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="product-section__header">
      <span>03</span>

      <div>
        <h2>What may have an ongoing cost</h2>

        <p>
          Some services cost money each time they are used. Those are treated
          separately from ownership of the application.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="plain-table">
      <div class="plain-table__row plain-table__head">
        <span>Service</span>
        <span>How it is handled</span>
      </div>

      <div class="plain-table__row">
        <span>Core application</span>
        <span>Purchased version</span>
      </div>

      <div class="plain-table__row">
        <span>Software updates</span>
        <span>Optional new versions</span>
      </div>

      <div class="plain-table__row">
        <span>AI services</span>
        <span>Usage based</span>
      </div>

      <div class="plain-table__row">
        <span>Other external APIs</span>
        <span>Usage based where applicable</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-section product-section--accent">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="product-section__header">
      <span>04</span>

      <div>
        <h2>After-hours answering</h2>

        <p>
          A planned part of the system is an AI-assisted answering service
          connected to the business account.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="answering-example">
      <div>
        <span>6:14 PM</span>
        <p>“What time do you open tomorrow?”</p>
        <strong>Answer automatically</strong>
      </div>

      <div>
        <span>8:37 PM</span>
        <p>“Can someone give me a price on replacing this?”</p>
        <strong>Record as a possible sales lead</strong>
      </div>

      <div>
        <span>11:52 PM</span>
        <p>“The repair you did today is leaking badly.”</p>
        <strong>Escalate to the appropriate person</strong>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="section-note">
      AI and telephone services depend on external providers and would therefore
      have usage costs.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-section">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="product-section__header">
      <span>05</span>

      <div>
        <h2>Try the application</h2>

        <p>
          The demos are there to show how individual parts of the application
          work. They do not require creating a business account.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="demo-list">
      <a href="/demo/customers">
        <span>Customer records</span>
        <span>Open demo →</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/demo/jobs">
        <span>Jobs and tasks</span>
        <span>Open demo →</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/demo/inventory">
        <span>Inventory</span>
        <span>Open demo →</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/demo/invoices">
        <span>Estimates and invoices</span>
        <span>Open demo →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="product-section signup-section">
  <div class="container signup-section__inner">
    <div>
      <h2>Create a business account</h2>

      <p>
        Business owners create the business first and are enrolled as its first
        user. Employees are added later through invitations from the business.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/signup" class="button button--primary"> Create Business </a>
  </div>
</section>
